==============================================================
1. What git puts in a hook's environment, in a NORMAL clone
==============================================================
cwd=/Users/nguyenanhkiet/Playground/flutter-starter
GIT_AUTHOR_DATE=@1790405877 +0700
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=kietna.work@gmail.com
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=koniz-dev
GIT_EDITOR=:
GIT_EXEC_PATH=/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/usr/libexec/git-core
GIT_INDEX_FILE=.git/index
GIT_PREFIX=

GIT_DIR is absent. That is why the hook works in a normal clone.
A worktree is the case where git exports an absolute GIT_DIR, because the
worktree's .git is a file pointing at <main>/.git/worktrees/<name>.

==============================================================
2. The leak, at the git level (instant, no Flutter involved)
==============================================================
$ git -C $FLUTTER_ROOT describe --tags
3.47.0

$ GIT_DIR=/Users/nguyenanhkiet/Playground/flutter-starter/.git git -C $FLUTTER_ROOT describe --tags
fatal: No tags can describe 'bedbeeb5f9cc6528f2c8876e6e5cee647f86bf35'.
Try --always, or create some tags.

An exported GIT_DIR overrides even an explicit -C. Flutter resolves its
own version through exactly this call, so inside a hook it reads THIS
repository's history and calls the answer the SDK version.

==============================================================
3. The leak, at the Flutter level
==============================================================
$ flutter --version
Flutter 3.47.0 • channel stable • https://github.com/flutter/flutter.git
Framework • revision 4cf2416426 (7 weeks ago) • 2026-08-11 11:53:49 -0700

$ GIT_DIR=/Users/nguyenanhkiet/Playground/flutter-starter/.git flutter --version     # what the hook sees in a worktree
Flutter 3.49.0-0.1.pre • channel [user-branch] • https://github.com/koniz-dev/flutter-starter.git
Framework • revision bedbeeb5f9 (30 seconds ago) • 2026-09-26 14:05:28 +0700

$ flutter --version                        # restoring the SDK's own stamp
Flutter 3.47.0 • channel stable • https://github.com/flutter/flutter.git
Framework • revision 4cf2416426 (7 weeks ago) • 2026-08-11 11:53:49 -0700

==============================================================
4. BEFORE vs AFTER, at the hook level, under a worktree-shaped env
==============================================================
PATH is shimmed so 'flutter' and 'dart' just report the environment they
were handed and exit 0. Nothing else about the hooks is changed.

--- origin/main's .githooks/pre-commit, with GIT_DIR exported:
Running pre-commit checks...
📝 Checking code formatting...
  [shim] dart format invoked with GIT_DIR=/Users/nguyenanhkiet/Playground/flutter-starter/.git
🔍 Running flutter analyze...
  [shim] flutter analyze invoked with GIT_DIR=/Users/nguyenanhkiet/Playground/flutter-starter/.git GIT_INDEX_FILE=/Users/nguyenanhkiet/Playground/flutter-starter/.git/index GIT_WORK_TREE=(unset)
✅ Pre-commit checks passed.
exit: 0

--- this branch's .githooks/pre-commit, same environment:
